nfstream (6.6.0~ds1) UNRELEASED; urgency=medium

  * New upstream release.
  * Delete vendorized code management from debian/rules: that's been
    integrated upstream in a slightly different way; their setup.py and
    the few submodules seem to be enough to build static libraries
    (libndpi.a and libpcap.a) and then the desired shared library
    (_lib_engine.abi3.so).
  * Delete vendor/* subdirectories.
  * Delete patch (no longer needed):
     - libgcrypt-update-gpg-error-detection.patch
  * Add patches:
     - avoid-pyproject-related-problems.diff
     - only-compile-with-build-action.diff
     - enable-parallel-builds.diff
     - avoid-tmp-dir.diff
     - adjust-engine-name.diff
  * Clean tmp/ accordingly (see avoid-tmp-dif.diff).
  * Clean other leftovers in the nDPI directory.
  * Delete the dh_python3 override, as the extension renaming step has
    become a no-op (the filename is static, and doesn't embed any
    information regarding the Python implementation/version).

 -- Cyril Brulebois <cyril@debamax.com>  Wed, 15 Apr 2026 14:41:46 +0200

nfstream (6.3.5~ds3) bookworm; urgency=medium

  * Add git build-dep.
  * Fix typo in debian/README.source
  * Enable quilt (build-dep and dh sequence).
  * Add libgcrypt-update-gpg-error-detection.patch to fix libgpg-error
    detection due to gpg-error-config's removal in Bookworm. Upstream m4
    macro from latest master branch, adding support for gpgrt-config.
  * Force parallelism with -j$(nproc) for all 4 subdirectory builds.
  * Set tar-ignore to an empty string via debian/source/options, since
    the source package needs to retain git metadata for the build to
    succeed.

 -- Cyril Brulebois <cyril@debamax.com>  Sat, 24 Jun 2023 06:57:40 +0200

